WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.350
The application holds documents, memory and tools. The model does not automatically receive everything.

2
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:14.200
The assembler selects three items for this inference. Everything else stays outside.

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:22.250
The decision depends on this specific input, not everything held by the application.

4
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:29.600
The prompt asks for the current policy on a twenty-day-old order.

5
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:36.450
Copy A allows thirty days. Rewording the prompt does not update that source.

6
00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:44.867
Current revision B allows fourteen days. With the same prompt, the evidence requires a different decision.

7
00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:52.217
Three passages appear relevant, but one belongs to another customer.

8
00:00:52.217 --> 00:00:59.383
The access boundary excludes it before utility is compared. Similarity grants no permission.

9
00:00:59.383 --> 00:01:06.733
Only eligible items can compete for space in the context.

10
00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:14.400
Context C0 contains a hypothesis about the failure. The test has not returned yet.

11
00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:21.250
The actual result contradicts that hypothesis. This observation did not exist in C0.

12
00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:28.600
The assembler puts the result in C1 and removes the invalidated hypothesis.

13
00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:35.950
Stable instructions enter at the start. Large files remain behind references.

14
00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:42.800
A new question triggers a read of the relevant file, not the whole repository.

15
00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:50.150
On-demand loading saves context but adds a read that can fail.

16
00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:57.500
An answer alone does not reveal which information the model received.

17
00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:04.350
The receipt keeps IDs, revisions and reasons for inclusion or exclusion.

18
00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:11.700
This separates missing evidence from evidence that was received but misused.

